Data Structures that Power Your Database
Consider the world’s simplest database, implemented as two Bash functions:
#!/bin/bash
db_set () {
    echo "$1,$2" >> database
}
db_get () {
    grep "^$1," database | sed -e "s/^$1,//" | tail -n 1
}
